- Technical Details
    - Tech Stack:
        - Bash scripts
        - tmux 3.4
        - fzf 0.44.1
    - Key Files:
        - bin/tm: Main dispatcher
        - bin/tm-picker: Interactive fzf session picker
        - bin/tm-cheatsheet: ANSI formatted cheatsheet
        - bin/tm-clip: Clipboard helper for copy-mode (xclip, wl-copy, termux-clipboard-set, pbcopy)
        - conf/tmux.conf: Shared tmux configuration (Ctrl+T prefix)
        - conf/profiles/*.conf: Per-machine profiles (laptop, server, phone) symlinked to ~/.tmux.conf.local
        - data/: loglog data files for commands, keybindings, cheatsheet
        - install.sh: Installs config, profile, symlinks, TPM bootstrap
    - Architecture Notes:
        - Data-driven: commands and keybindings defined in data/ files
        - Ctrl+T prefix replaces Ctrl+B
        - Alt+Arrows for resize (Fn+Arrows not portable on Linux)
        - Mouse wheel enters copy mode for scrolling history
        - Role-agnostic shared config + per-machine profile sourced last via ~/.tmux.conf.local
        - Machine identity in the status bar comes from @machine_color and optional @machine_label
        - TPM plugin loading is gated by @enable_plugins, set in the profile
        - install.sh detects Termux (pkg/$PREFIX) vs Linux (apt/~/.local/bin)
        - Host-specific values (hostnames, machine names) stay out of the repo

